Example 1 – simple multiplication
  Simplify &frac{3}{x} × &frac{x}{5}
  Multiply numerators: 3 × x = 3x
  Multiply denominators: x × 5 = 5x
  Cancel x: &frac{3x}{5x} = &frac{3}{5}
  &frac{3}{5}
  (Cancel any common factors between numerator and denominator.)

Example 2 – division
  Simplify &frac{4}{x} ÷ &frac{2}{x}
  Flip second fraction: &frac{4}{x} × &frac{x}{2}
  Multiply: &frac{4x}{2x}
  Cancel: &frac{4x}{2x} = 2
  = 2
  (Keep the first, flip the second, then multiply.)

✓ To divide fractions, flip the second and multiply
✗ &frac{2}{x} × &frac{3}{x} = &frac{6}{x}
✓ &frac{x+1}{x+2} × &frac{x+2}{x+3} = &frac{x+1}{x+3}
✗ &frac{a}{b} ÷ &frac{c}{d} = &frac{a}{b} × &frac{c}{d}
✓ You should factorise before cancelling
